          {
            "url": "https://generesolver.io/fhir/StructureDefinition/etiology-classification",
            "valueString": "single_gene — The patient presents with a constellation of symptoms including kidney failure, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, burning limb pain, abdominal pain, and intolerance to temperature extremes, along with a family history suggestive of an inherited disorder affecting multiple organ systems. This pattern points towards a disorder caused by a mutation in a single gene that affects multiple tissues or pathways.. The combination of kidney disease (small echogenic kidneys), hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, and neuropathic pain (burning limbs) in the patient, along with similar symptoms in his daughter and maternal cousin, strongly suggests an inherited condition affecting multiple organ systems. This pattern is characteristic of single-gene disorders, often involving metabolic pathways or structural proteins expressed in various tissues. The specific combination of symptoms is highly suggestive of Fabry disease, a lysosomal storage disorder caused by mutations in the GLA gene"
          }
        ]
